  "security_scope": "Original WIP finite counter action, not ready for real funds. Accepts exactly (owner48_atom StateTruth), validates the old canonical u64 even though it is discarded, and returns the same opaque ephemeral tree with count zero and one fixed-intent AGG_SIG_ME condition. Curry the owner as one 48-byte atom before funding the action-layer instance. The signature is a coin/network-bound reset capability and does not bind the complete batch or action order. The explicit Cons output is an action result, not a condition list or complete standalone coin puzzle. Canonical action-layer, finalizer and singleton host composition is separate from these original Rust/Chialisp/Rue actions. Standalone VM output does not establish signature validity, complete-spend acceptance, a general registry/slot demo, live Testnet11 use or compiler preservation.",
